        "id": "f5d01391e90b2e1d5d1c34a9d59ea529a10a55c3",
        "message": "feat!: fail closed when a response content type is not declared in the content map\n\nWhen a route declares a per-media-type (`content`) response schema but the\nresponse `Content-Type` is neither a declared key nor `*/*`, the payload was\npreviously serialized with a raw `JSON.stringify`. That fallback bypassed the\nresponse schema and could expose fields the schema was meant to strip.\n\nThe route response path now fails closed. If the response content type is not\ndeclared and no `*/*` catch-all matches, `getSchemaSerializer` throws\n`FST_ERR_MISSING_CONTENTTYPE_SERIALIZATION_FN` and the reply is a `500`,\nsurfacing the misconfiguration instead of silently returning unsanitized data.\n\nThe error handler call path is unchanged: it still resolves the default error\nserializer (requesting `failClosed: false`), so error responses are unaffected.",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-19T11:25:54Z",
        "tree_id": "335d377d1d1abdf85112cb9e989cffa8fb4c61af"
      },
